{"lines": ["So what is left? Two sounds.", "Upsweep. A long train of narrow-band, upward-sweeping sounds, each about three seconds. It was already there when NOAA began recording in August of 1991. Loud enough to be recorded across the Pacific. Located roughly at fifty-four degrees south, one hundred and forty west, near volcanic seismicity. It peaks in spring and autumn, and nobody is sure if that is the source or the sound's path. NOAA calls its origin unresolved. It has been getting quieter since 1991, but you can still detect it.", "And one animal. A voice at fifty-two hertz in the North Pacific, first detected by a team from Woods Hole in 1989. Blue whales call between ten and thirty-nine hertz. Fin whales, about twenty. The call has been tracked every year since, through at least 2014. It deepened over the years, to about fifty hertz by 2004. And the animal was never confirmed by sight.", "In 2021, a documentary said it had found a possible answer, a blue-and-fin whale hybrid. It is a possibility. Not yet a confirmed fact.", "Rule seven. Say unresolved out loud. That is how the next person knows where to listen."], "words": [["So", 0.0, 0.16], ["what", 0.16, 0.34], ["is", 0.34, 0.48], ["left?", 0.48, 0.74], ["Two", 0.74, 1.2], ["sounds.", 1.2, 1.6], ["Upsweep.", 1.6, 3.3], ["A", 3.3, 3.36], ["long", 3.36, 3.52], ["train", 3.52, 3.9], ["of", 3.9, 4.12], ["narrow-band,", 4.12, 4.82], ["upward-sweeping", 4.82, 5.52], ["sounds,", 5.52, 6.08], ["each", 6.54, 6.66], ["about", 6.66, 6.94], ["three", 6.94, 7.28], ["seconds.", 7.28, 7.66], ["It", 8.3, 8.4], ["was", 8.4, 8.48], ["already", 8.48, 8.76], ["there", 8.76, 9.06], ["when", 9.06, 9.26], ["NOAA", 9.26, 9.44], ["began", 9.44, 9.8], ["recording", 9.8, 10.26], ["in", 10.26, 10.58], ["August", 10.58, 10.84], ["of", 10.84, 11.1], ["1991.", 11.1, 11.94], ["Loud", 12.78, 13.1], ["enough", 13.1, 13.36], ["to", 13.36, 13.62], ["be", 13.62, 13.74], ["recorded", 13.74, 14.1], ["across", 14.1, 14.42], ["the", 14.42, 14.7],